cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "EIGEN: Cleaning stock correlation matrices with random matrix theory"
authors:
  - family-names: Platania
    given-names: Hunter
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/HunterPlatania/eigen"
abstract: >-
  Eigenvalue clipping of a 102-stock correlation matrix (2010 to 2026),
  tested out of sample over 176 monthly rebalances of minimum-variance
  portfolios. On this data, cleaning does not beat the raw matrix: raw had
  the lowest realized risk (13.01%, vs 14.59% clipped and 13.39%
  clipped-adjusted), and all three matrices underestimated risk by about 50%.